WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.833 --> 00:00:35.000


2
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:40.500
<b>Until now, Arjuna was fixated on the idea that</b>
<b>what they were about to do was wrong.</b>

3
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.250
<b>Here,</b>

4
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:44.375
<b>for the first time, another layer unfolds,</b>

5
00:00:44.375 --> 00:00:50.125
<b>and we get a glimpse that Arjuna's mind</b>
<b>isn't set on not fighting,</b>

6
00:00:50.125 --> 00:00:51.000
<b>but</b>

7
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.125
<b>rather caught in a great dilemma.</b>

8
00:00:53.125 --> 00:00:54.666
<b>Here, he says,</b>

9
00:00:54.666 --> 00:00:58.833
<b>"I don't know if conquering the Kauravas is right,</b>

10
00:00:58.833 --> 00:00:59.375
<b>or</b>

11
00:00:59.375 --> 00:01:02.083
<b>if being defeated by them would be right.</b>

12
00:01:02.083 --> 00:01:08.125
<b>I might not even think it proper to live</b>
<b>after killing the Kauravas,</b>

13
00:01:08.125 --> 00:01:09.291
<b>but they...</b>

14
00:01:09.291 --> 00:01:11.833
<b>they stand ready for this war."</b>

15
00:01:12.541 --> 00:01:16.750


16
00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:18.500
<b>Arjuna has made many arguments,</b>

17
00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:19.666
<b>counterarguments,</b>

18
00:01:19.666 --> 00:01:20.833
<b>raised many questions,</b>

19
00:01:20.833 --> 00:01:24.041
<b>and even answered some himself.</b>

20
00:01:24.041 --> 00:01:26.458
<b>After so much turmoil in his mind,</b>

21
00:01:26.458 --> 00:01:30.750
<b>here, for the first time,</b>
<b>Arjuna is opening up a bit more.</b>

22
00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:34.458
<b>He's trying to express that the truth is,</b>

23
00:01:34.458 --> 00:01:38.541
<b>he doesn't know which of these two options</b>
<b>would be right for him.</b>

24
00:01:38.541 --> 00:01:39.791
<b>To fight,</b>

25
00:01:39.791 --> 00:01:42.000
<b>or to abandon the war.</b>

26
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.125
<b>The dilemma is this: </b>

27
00:01:43.125 --> 00:01:45.875
<b>if he fights and wins,</b>

28
00:01:45.875 --> 00:01:52.125
<b>he'll have to live with the sin of killing</b>
<b>his family members and elders for life.</b>

29
00:01:52.125 --> 00:01:57.041
<b>If he fights and dies heroically,</b>
<b>his duty will be fulfilled,</b>

30
00:01:57.041 --> 00:01:58.541
<b>he won't incur sin,</b>

31
00:01:58.541 --> 00:02:01.500
<b>and he'll attain heaven.</b>

32
00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:03.333
<b>This seems right to think about,</b>

33
00:02:03.333 --> 00:02:04.083
<b>but</b>

34
00:02:04.083 --> 00:02:07.083
<b>if he fights, he must do so wholeheartedly</b>

35
00:02:07.083 --> 00:02:09.458
<b>only then will it be duty fulfilled.</b>

36
00:02:09.458 --> 00:02:14.541
<b>And in that case, the possibility isn't just of</b>
<b>a heroic death, but also of victory.</b>

37
00:02:14.541 --> 00:02:19.541
<b>The dilemma of the sin of killing</b>
<b>his own people looms again.</b>

38
00:02:19.541 --> 00:02:21.500
<b>If he abandons the war,</b>

39
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:23.666
<b>then why did they come this far?</b>

40
00:02:23.666 --> 00:02:25.625
<b>In this case, he'll fail his duty,</b>

41
00:02:25.625 --> 00:02:28.375
<b>and might have to beg for alms his whole life.</b>

42
00:02:28.375 --> 00:02:35.250
<b>And the doubt whether this decision to</b>
<b>abandon was right or not will never leave him.</b>

43
00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:39.500
<b>It's not just Arjuna; many others</b>
<b>are involved in this war too.</b>

44
00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:42.000
<b>War is no laughing matter.</b>

45
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:47.333
<b>In this situation, you can understand</b>
<b>how serious this predicament is!</b>

46
00:02:48.041 --> 00:02:51.833


47
00:02:51.833 --> 00:02:54.750
<b>Not entirely exhausted,</b>

48
00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:55.791
<b>but</b>

49
00:02:55.791 --> 00:03:01.250
<b>Arjuna's reservoir of arguments and</b>
<b>counter-arguments has certainly diminished.</b>

50
00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:11.875
<b>Perhaps you too can now see beyond</b>
<b>the outer layer, to the confusion within him.</b>

51
00:03:11.875 --> 00:03:12.458
<b>Confusion,</b>

52
00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:13.708
<b>uncertainty, </b>

53
00:03:13.708 --> 00:03:14.750
<b> dilemma</b>

54
00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:17.958
<b>these are integral parts of human life,</b>

55
00:03:17.958 --> 00:03:20.458
<b>everyone must face them.</b>

56
00:03:20.458 --> 00:03:24.458
<b>At every age, we must face them.</b>

57
00:03:24.458 --> 00:03:26.708
<b>Which school to study in,</b>

58
00:03:26.708 --> 00:03:29.208
<b>which profession to choose,</b>

59
00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:33.625
<b>whom to marry and make a life partner.</b>

60
00:03:33.625 --> 00:03:36.958
<b>Countless dilemmas will arise.</b>

61
00:03:36.958 --> 00:03:45.000
<b>The first step to resolving any dilemma is</b>
<b>to understand it clearly in your own words.</b>

62
00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.375
<b>For this, it's necessary</b>

63
00:03:47.375 --> 00:03:50.458
<b>to peel back each layer of the dilemma,</b>

64
00:03:50.458 --> 00:03:53.666
<b>and this peeling happens through questions</b>

65
00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:57.250
<b>you must ask yourself.</b>

66
00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:00.375
<b>One by one.</b>

67
00:04:00.375 --> 00:04:02.083
<b>What is the dilemma?</b>

68
00:04:02.083 --> 00:04:05.458
<b>In which different directions is it pulling you?</b>

69
00:04:05.458 --> 00:04:07.916
<b>Assess each of these directions,</b>

70
00:04:07.916 --> 00:04:11.291
<b>what are the options if you go in this direction?</b>

71
00:04:11.291 --> 00:04:15.083
<b>If you choose this direction, this option, </b>

72
00:04:15.083 --> 00:04:18.750
<b>what will be its destination down the line?</b>

73
00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:21.583
<b>Its end?</b>

74
00:04:21.583 --> 00:04:26.250
<b>When you imaginatively observe</b>
<b>all these directions,</b>

75
00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:31.166
<b>when you weigh each of</b>
<b>these options one by one,</b>

76
00:04:31.166 --> 00:04:34.041
<b>certainty will start to form,</b>

77
00:04:34.041 --> 00:04:36.083
<b>the fog will begin to clear,</b>

78
00:04:36.083 --> 00:04:39.625
<b>the path will start to appear clearer than before.</b>

79
00:04:40.166 --> 00:04:43.875


80
00:04:43.875 --> 00:04:45.958
<b>The bigger the dilemma,</b>

81
00:04:45.958 --> 00:04:49.291
<b>the deeper you need to look within.</b>

82
00:04:49.291 --> 00:04:50.708
<b>Imagine</b>

83
00:04:50.708 --> 00:04:55.166
<b>there's a maze inside you,</b>

84
00:04:55.166 --> 00:04:59.666
<b>with various tunnels of different options,</b>

85
00:04:59.666 --> 00:05:04.916
<b>and at the entrance of each tunnel</b>
<b>is a lock of questions,</b>

86
00:05:04.916 --> 00:05:06.375
<b>which opens</b>

87
00:05:06.375 --> 00:05:09.416
<b> by giving honest answers to yourself.</b>

88
00:05:09.416 --> 00:05:18.541
<b>By imaginatively opening these doors</b>
<b>one by one, you can fully see this maze,</b>

89
00:05:18.541 --> 00:05:20.583
<b>and solve it.</b>

90
00:05:20.583 --> 00:05:21.791
<b>But sometimes,</b>

91
00:05:21.791 --> 00:05:29.333
<b>when our decisions affect family or society,</b>

92
00:05:29.333 --> 00:05:34.250
<b>this maze becomes even more complex.</b>

93
00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:35.291
<b>In such cases,</b>

94
00:05:35.291 --> 00:05:38.083
<b>it's necessary to think even more deeply,</b>

95
00:05:38.083 --> 00:05:39.375
<b>because</b>

96
00:05:39.375 --> 00:05:44.958
<b>facing the consequences of your own mistake</b>
<b>might not be as difficult,</b>

97
00:05:44.958 --> 00:05:46.375
<b>but</b>

98
00:05:46.375 --> 00:05:55.000
<b>if it negatively impacts your family</b>
<b>or others because of you,</b>

99
00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:59.166
<b>this guilt stays with you for a long time.</b>

100
00:05:59.166 --> 00:06:03.875
<b>Just keep this in mind and</b>
<b>be a little more cautious,</b>

101
00:06:03.875 --> 00:06:05.541
<b>but don't panic at all.</b>

102
00:06:05.541 --> 00:06:07.375
<b>Just know that</b>

103
00:06:07.375 --> 00:06:11.541
<b>the weight of countless questions</b>
<b>is completely natural,</b>

104
00:06:11.541 --> 00:06:16.166
<b>especially when others depend on you.</b>

105
00:06:16.166 --> 00:06:18.250
<b>Arjuna is a great sage,  </b>

106
00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:20.375
<b>a great warrior,</b>

107
00:06:20.375 --> 00:06:21.333
<b>but</b>

108
00:06:21.333 --> 00:06:24.583
<b>still, this time is very heavy for him.</b>

109
00:06:24.583 --> 00:06:26.000
<b>And similarly,</b>

110
00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:32.750
<b>know that your situation isn't</b>
<b>as dire as this great war,</b>

111
00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:37.958
<b>not as heavy as the thought</b>
<b>of killing your own kin.</b>

112
00:06:37.958 --> 00:06:44.333
<b>If these teachings of the Gita can resolve</b>
<b>Arjuna's huge dilemma, </b>

113
00:06:44.333 --> 00:06:48.791
<b>they will surely solve your confusion too.</b>

114
00:06:48.791 --> 00:06:54.875
<b>In each teaching, there's a key hidden to unlock</b>
<b>the maze of your mind.</b>

115
00:06:54.875 --> 00:06:57.583
<b>Just stay with me.</b>

116
00:06:58.333 --> 00:07:02.791


117
00:07:02.791 --> 00:07:05.375
<b>The options before Arjuna</b>

118
00:07:05.375 --> 00:07:09.541
<b>each have some good and some bad.</b>

119
00:07:09.541 --> 00:07:12.375
<b>He's weighing each option,</b>

120
00:07:12.375 --> 00:07:17.166
<b>assessing their long-term consequences.</b>

121
00:07:17.166 --> 00:07:21.583
<b>And this is what will help you in professional life.</b>

122
00:07:21.583 --> 00:07:23.125
<b>Weighing options,</b>

123
00:07:23.125 --> 00:07:26.500
<b>considering their long-term effects,</b>

124
00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:28.958
<b> and then making decisions.</b>

125
00:07:28.958 --> 00:07:36.041
<b>Making the right decisions with long-term</b>
<b>impact - this is a big part of leadership.</b>

126
00:07:36.041 --> 00:07:36.791
<b>But</b>

127
00:07:36.791 --> 00:07:40.708
<b>here, Arjuna is teaching another lesson.</b>

128
00:07:40.708 --> 00:07:43.583
<b>It's about seeking advice.</b>

129
00:07:43.583 --> 00:07:48.416
<b>Seeking advice and</b>
<b>being humble enough to do so.</b>

130
00:07:48.416 --> 00:07:53.375
<b>Humility is a great sign of the truly wise.</b>

131
00:07:53.375 --> 00:07:55.833
<b>They don't get caught up in ego;</b>

132
00:07:55.833 --> 00:07:58.041
<b>when they get badly stuck,</b>

133
00:07:58.041 --> 00:08:03.583
<b>they bow their heads and start learning</b>
<b>something new on that subject.</b>

134
00:08:03.583 --> 00:08:07.083
<b>They seek advice from experienced people.</b>

135
00:08:07.083 --> 00:08:07.916
<b>Just as</b>

136
00:08:07.916 --> 00:08:10.416
<b>Arjuna is doing now,</b>

137
00:08:10.416 --> 00:08:11.333
<b>with me.</b>

138
00:08:11.333 --> 00:08:15.250
<b>And for this advice, either someone</b>
<b>is present before you,</b>

139
00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:19.833
<b>or books contain the essence of</b>
<b>hundreds of years of experience. </b>

140
00:08:19.833 --> 00:08:22.708
<b>Have you ever thought about this?</b>

141
00:08:22.708 --> 00:08:26.250
<b>How much immense wealth of</b>
<b>knowledge is hidden in these libraries,</b>

142
00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:29.666
<b>between those pages?</b>

143
00:08:29.666 --> 00:08:31.458
<b>Stay humble.</b>

144
00:08:31.458 --> 00:08:36.083
<b>Try to understand a dilemma yourself,</b>

145
00:08:36.083 --> 00:08:36.875
<b>but</b>

146
00:08:36.875 --> 00:08:42.125
<b>don't hesitate to seek help from</b>
<b>someone experienced if needed.</b>

147
00:08:42.125 --> 00:08:43.250
<b>And yes, </b>

148
00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:47.000
<b>don't deprive yourself of</b>
<b>this ocean of knowledge.</b>

149
00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:49.833
<b>Keep reading good books constantly.</b>

150
00:08:49.833 --> 00:08:51.458
<b>They contain experience,</b>

151
00:08:51.458 --> 00:08:53.791
<b>they have keys to many locks.</b>

